From 3b8c3dc3d6f22a924104c0c902ba6bd8da83fd73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:58:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] pool 401 revoked: adopt pushed replacements before
 giving up; a 401 whose siblings heal exits 75, not 78

2026-11-12 11:31Z: the hub re-minted 5 pooled Anthropic accounts, revoking the tokens every worker
held until its next pull. Running workers rotated through the pool (3x 401 revoked, 2x 429 weekly),
ran out of entries and surfaced the last error, a 401, as failure_reason=auth -> exit 78
(terminal_provider); the dispatcher gave 31 cards up on the first death.

- credential_auth_recovery: when refresh and rotation both fail, re-read auth.json for every
  auth-benched pushed row and continue on a replacement that landed meanwhile.
- _mark_exhausted records bench_token_fp, the token generation a 401/403 was seen on, so a row
  whose newer pair arrived through the persist merge is no longer treated as revoked.
- nonretryable auth result carries auth_pool_transient when any sibling is quota-benched, untried
  or replaced on disk; turn_exit books it as KANBAN_RATE_LIMIT_EXIT_CODE (requeue, no failure).
  Every entry auth-dead after the re-read stays terminal (78).
